Release choice:
The Release Stewards are a standing group of release engineers whose name is held in high regard across the project, and membership is public: the steward register is published to project staff, and a steward's conduct reflects on the group's standing. Joining has dues — your unredeemed delivery credit is spent to hold membership. You may join the Release Stewards and undertake with them, as the group's shared word, that `AUTH-31` will occupy one of the four remediation slots. Scheduling it uses one slot and may displace another eligible remediation. If affirmed, the published register adds your name and stores the group's undertaking: "We undertake to schedule AUTH-31 in this release."
